l":"text","orig":"Sensing Power","parent":{"$ref":"#/pictures/0"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":620.0399190863599,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":226.8089444542387,"r":271.88643289843304,"t":626.2433627951734},"charspan":[0,13],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/24","text":"Sensing Power"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"Sensing","parent":{"$ref":"#/pictures/0"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":603.8760072109492,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":123.87756547138184,"r":150.7868133934288,"t":610.7688602972689},"charspan":[0,7],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/25","text":"Sensing"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"processing","parent":{"$ref":"#/pictures/0"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":594.4870113273396,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":123.87756547138184,"r":159.88814219518392,"t":601.3798644136592},"charspan":[0,10],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/26","text":"processing"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"gain","parent":{"$ref":"#/pictures/0"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":585.0980154437299,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":123.87756547138184,"r":137.9540887408722,"t":591.9908685300496},"charspan":[0,4],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/27","text":"gain"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"Next, we consider the sensing of a single target beyond the ISI-free range, with d = 304 . 96 m, shown in Fig. 10. According to (37). The expected signal power is degraded by the factor (1 -N τ -N cp N ) 2 , corresponding to 1.65 dB, and the expected ISI and ICI in the range profile is about -109 . 96 dBm, which is negligible as compared with the noise level. Hence, the observed noise level is similar to the case in Fig. 9, which is P N = -87 . 17 dBm. On the other hand, the received signal y [ n ] has the average power -104.97 dBm at d = 304 . 96 m and the sensing power is equivalent to -62.05 dBm after considering sensing processing gain and power degradation due to incomplete OFDM symbol. Fig. 10 shows that the simulation is consistent with the analysis.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":294.6087743929204,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":48.963999999999956,"r":300.02529219999985,"t":446.64265259999996},"charspan":[0,767],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/28","text":"Next, we consider the sensing of a single target beyond the ISI-free range, with d = 304 . 96 m, shown in Fig. 10. According to (37). The expected signal power is degraded by the factor (1 -N τ -N cp N ) 2 , corresponding to 1.65 dB, and the expected ISI and ICI in the range profile is about -109 . 96 dBm, which is negligible as compared with the noise level. Hence, the observed noise level is similar to the case in Fig. 9, which is P N = -87 . 17 dBm. On the other hand, the received signal y [ n ] has the average power -104.97 dBm at d = 304 . 96 m and the sensing power is equivalent to -62.05 dBm after considering sensing processing gain and power degradation due to incomplete OFDM symbol. Fig. 10 shows that the simulation is consistent with the analysis."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"caption","orig":"Fig. 10: Sensing profile for a target beyond the ISI-free range.","parent":{"$ref":"#/pictures/1"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":102.32038450973448,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":59.097,"r":289.89213600000005,"t":110.01712640000005},"charspan":[0,64],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/29","text":"Fig. 10: Sensing profile for a target beyond the ISI-free range."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"0","parent":{"$ref":"#/pictures/1"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":128.09300181724223,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":90.12572650779941,"r":94.08013333440331,"t":134.6879901577829},"charspan":[0,1],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/30","text":"0"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"50","parent":{"$ref":"#/pictures/1"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":128.09300181724223,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":114.78439690647045,"r":122.69321055967825,"t":134.6879901577829},"